//? Title: Phase estimation: actual counting-register amplitudes
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The supplied phase already represents an eigenstate’s phase kickback; this
classical program does not infer an unknown unitary or prepare its eigenstate.
It applies the actual native Hadamards, phase gates and inverse QFT to a state
vector. The historical measured field is the first strict maximum of computed
probabilities, not a sampled quantum measurement. State storage is exponential
in the counting-bit count. The original dyadic3/8 and nondyadic0.3 fixtures are
retained, with no external dataset.

$$ a_k=2^{-t/2}\exp(2\pi i\varphi k),\qquad P(m)=\left|2^{-t}\sum_{k=0}^{2^t-1}\exp(2\pi i k(\varphi-m/2^t))\right|^2. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/phase_estimation_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/phase_estimation.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = dm::algorithms::phase_estimation_trace(3, .375);
    std::print("\n| basis | actual uniform real part | actual kickback real | kickback imaginary | actual " "final real | final imaginary | actual probability |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.distribution.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   t.after_hadamards[i].real(), t.after_kickback[i].real(),
                   t.after_kickback[i].imag(), t.after_inverse_qft[i].real(),
                   t.after_inverse_qft[i].imag(), t.distribution[i]);

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual uniform amplitude[1]\n{:.6f}",
                       t.after_hadamards[1].real()));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual kicked amplitude[1]\n{:.6f} + {:.6f} i",
                       t.after_kickback[1].real(), t.after_kickback[1].imag()));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual deterministic mode\nindex {}, P={:.6f}",
                       t.result.measured, t.result.probability));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/phase_estimation_tiny.svg");
}
```
